    <statement><p>Evaluate <m>\frac{\,d}{\,dt}{\bf r}(g(t))</m> using the Chain Rule:</p>
<p><m>{\bf r}(t)=\left\lt e^t,e^{3 t},-3\right&gt;, \ \ g(t)=2 t+6</m></p>
<p><m>\frac{\,d}{\,dt}{\bf r}(g(t))=\langle</m><fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0001"/>,<fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0002"/>
,<fillin characters="20" name="AnSwEr0003"/><m>\rangle</m></p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>2e^{2t+6}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>6e^{3\mathopen{}\left(2t+6\right)}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>0</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><m>\bf r\it'(t)=\frac{\,d}{\,dt}\left\lt e^t,e^{3 t},-3\right&gt;=\left\lt e^t,3 e^{3 t},0\right&gt;</m>



<m>g'(t)=\frac{\,d}{\,dt}\left(2 t+6\right)=2</m>



Using the Chain Rule we get:



<m>\frac{\,d}{\,dt}\bf r\it(g(t))=g'(t) \bf r\it'(g(t))=2\left\lt e^{2 t+6},3 e^{3\left(2 t+6\right)},0\right&gt;=\left\lt 2 e^{2 t+6}, 6 e^{3\left(2 t+6\right)},0\right&gt;</m>



</solution>
